WEBVTT

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.070
Here's a letter I received this morning.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.990
Dear sir, in answer to your request for a report on the Aritar district,

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:20.300
there is no improvement in conditions, the land is unproductive and...

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.060
So my Aritar plea is worthless, eh?

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.040
According to this.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.330
You mean to say that land is all left of the Abbott estate?

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.160
He demasked about that.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:29.980
In other words...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.450
I'm broke.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:36.140
Well, I had a lot of fun spending it while it lasted.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.400
Going broke may be the best thing that ever happened to you, Jack.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:41.870
There's a glorious opportunity in the West.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.160
You don't think I'm going out to the woolly wilds of Arizona and Utah

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.360
and rebuild the Abbott fortune, do you?

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:49.490
Why not?

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.100
You never know what you may find in the desert.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.840
I know what I'd find all right.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.990
Snakes and rocks and cows and sand.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.470
And I don't like any of those things.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:01:59.960
You might also...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.130
find a chance to use your expensive education you studied geology didn't you yes but only because

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:13.260
it gave me more time for other things now see here jack you might as well make up your mind to do

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:21.260
something well i'm not going out in the desert to do it cargo's good enough for me yes i suppose it

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:27.040
is i never thought i'd live to see an abbot who was afraid to go out and claim what was rightfully his

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.850
no matter what the danger but why

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.640
Try to claim worthless property.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.780
What do you mean, danger?

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.790
Suppose I'm going to tell you that I thought you were being robbed.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.590
I'd say it was beginning to sound exciting.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:44.590
Well, I've already written Holderness, your manager out there, to turn everything over to you.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.040
How do you know I'm going?

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:50.630
You're an abbot, aren't you?

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.310
All right, Judd.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:59.970
But don't be surprised if I come back wearing a five-gallon hat in one of those western gals.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.970
Those get-ups, as you call them, are worn by real men.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.420
Remember that.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.340
All right, Judge. Goodbye.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:06.720
Goodbye.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:28.780
Into thy merciful hands, O infinite power, I commend my son.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.100
Thy will be done.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:37.750
I can't help it, David.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.740
He was so young, so strong.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:42.750
I didn't think that.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:46.320
My daughter, it's not for us to question.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.190
About time someone started questioning.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:52.640
Where are you going, David?

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.180
To get hold of this.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:55.570
I forbid it.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.320
You're always forbidding.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.910
No, David, this is not the time.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.110
Why isn't it?

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.970
For years, holiness has been robbing us,

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.850
driving us further and further into this dead...

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:05.250
My brothers.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.970
What have you done about it? Nothing.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:11.890
After all, your father has no real proof that Holderness was responsible for the killings.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.560
I have all the proof I need, Thornton.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.030
Brother's calling me to even things for him.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.050
And if you don't,

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.060
Violence is not the way to settle things, my son.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.560
I found that out years ago.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.680
I killed a man without first having proof that he was the one who wronged me.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.180
That must never happen again.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.060
A day of judgment always comes.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.120
You've been telling me that ever since Adam was killed.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:39.940
When is it coming?

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:41.510
Who knows, baby?

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:43.750
Maybe at this very moment.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.920
A noose might be settling on the neck of it.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:48.400
Henry Holden.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.170
Stay right here, my boy.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.370
Here comes your friend Thornton, chick.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.220
Friend of mine.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:29.220
Where are you heading?

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.310
None of your business.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.020
Thank you.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:40.440
What's up, Matt?

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:40.780
Alright.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.380
What do you two fellas want?

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:47.680
Nebraska and me just wanted to make sure everything was all right.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.500
It's all right. He's working for me.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.310
Why didn't you tell us?

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:55.360
I only tell people what they're supposed to know.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.580
I'll get out and wait till I call you.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.800
Why didn't you tell him? He might have started something.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:10.180
My business with you.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:12.290
You're getting smarter, Snap.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:13.400
Sure I am.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.550
Old man may have just made me foreman.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:16.940
That's fine.

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:20.070
Why, everything will be easy for us at the Oasis now.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.760
Not as far as you and I are concerned.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.840
I came in here to tell you that I'm quitting.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:26.920
Quitting what?

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.540
Playing the game with you.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:29.990
From now on, I'm...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.200
shooting square with the nabs.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:34.850
That sounds funny, coming from a man who killed Solmab.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.160
I couldn't help that.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.410
It was either him or me when he found out I was working for you.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:43.950
Do you think the Navs would accept that as an excuse if they knew?

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.160
You can't quit me.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.140
You're in too deep.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.000
Have a drink.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.970
And let's not have any more talk about quitting.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:15.400
What is the situation at the Oasis?

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:18.620
The old man's cattle are doing fine.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.300
Over a thousand head on the West Range alone.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.580
Well, this is going to be a profitable year.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:25.360
Thank you.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:26.420
I'll give you

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:29.990
An extra hundred, this.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.360
time.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:34.920
And we'll charge that to the removing of Saul Nair.

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.400
Sometimes I wish I'd never seen you.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:45.320
If you hadn't, you'd still be just a poor cow and struggling for a few hours.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:47.440
Well, at least I wouldn't be a double-crosser.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:48.750
And a killer.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.200
Take that with you, if you like.

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.490
Are you sure there ain't even a postal card for me to go for face?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.380
That little waitress over in Granite promised to write me.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.580
I told you, I ain't finished sorting the mail yet.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.100
These are all for the boss.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.740
The mail writer just came in.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.510
This one's from Chicago. It's from the lawyer.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.110
Well, you can go.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.000
Yes, sir.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:47.080
Strick.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:47.750
Yes?

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:49.740
Send Nebraska in here.

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:55.680
Yes, Nebraska, the boss wants you.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.380
I want you to meet a man for me.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.360
You'll find him somewhere on the trail between here and the junction.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:11.960
Wait until he comes along.

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.930
Sure, boss. I'll guide him in.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.220
I don't want that man to reach White Sage.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:19.280
You understand?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:21.850
His name is, uh...

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:22.530
Wait a minute.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:28.020
If that's the kind of job it is, then Chick's a better man for her than I am.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:29.960
What am I paying you for?

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:37.380
fighting not murder you're not getting a little bit yellow i guess you know that i'm always ready

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:43.090
to take plenty of short chances to earn my wages but the other fella's got to have an even break

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:51.910
hold even break nebraska that's him you might try being that way yourself sometimes chick

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:59.980
it'll be a change for you one like you in this outfit is enough i ain't

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:05.040
particular how I earn my pay. What's the name of this man you don't want to get here?

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:11.280
Sometimes I think you enjoy your work. Dollar's a dollar. Who is he?

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:18.880
No, his name is John Abbott. John Abbott. That's an easy name to remember.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:50.480
view from up here huh yeah mighty decent of you to guide me up here i never found my way alone

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:59.380
don't mention it i'm glad i had the chance where's the town uh just look down over that ledge and you

00:10:59.380 --> 00:10:59.960
can see where you're

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.320
Gone.

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:27.070
Me.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:29.390
Oh no.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:35.140
What did you say your name was?

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:37.830
You asked me that before.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:39.040
Abbott, I told you.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:40.040
John Abbott.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:48.120
I just wanted to make sure I ain't making no mistake.

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:54.130
That was a shot.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:55.990
Maybe someone's hunting.

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.490
Up there on Satan's Pass with a pistol.

00:11:58.940 --> 00:11:59.580
Nothing to hunt.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.340
a grasshopper up there.

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:41.520
Send the quicksign, David!

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:42.720
Hilarious!

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:03.480
I'm ready.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.060
Yeah, practically it's whining in the heart right now.

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:33.200
I wonder who done it.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:34.960
Death in this desert always means holiness.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.670
He needs our help, no matter who he is.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:39.420
Bring him out, lad.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:57.020
Well, how was your passion today, Miriam?

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:58.300
About the same, father.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:13:59.440
No better, no worse.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.570
You pull through, my child.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:06.090
The same power that delivered him from his enemies will restore him to hell.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:08.260
Enemies.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:09.800
Father.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:14.400
You need have no fear of enemies here, my son.

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:16.230
You're with friends.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:18.530
What is your name?

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.410
last man who asked me that.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:23.930
tried to kill me.

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:27.120
Never mind, it doesn't matter.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:29.890
We judge a man here by his deeds.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:30.920
It's not by his name.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:34.570
Rest easy and we'll have you on your feet in no time.

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.980
I don't know how I can repay you.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:06.990
We missed you last night.

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:08.390
Where were you, my lad?

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:11.040
Why, uh, on the West Range.

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:13.620
The stock is crowding seeping wells,

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:15.140
and some of them should be driven out.

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:18.900
Didn't look that way to me last time I was up there.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:23.040
That red eye you've been drinking makes you see double.

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.020
Oh, leave me alone, will you?

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:25.540
You know I've stopped drinking.

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.430
Sure are paying a lot of attention to him.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:50.280
Who is he?

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.700
Another stranger lost in the desert.

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:55.710
Why does your father bring strays around here?

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.160
This man might be anything.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.900
What difference does that make? He needed our help.

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:05.530
Oh, snap. You've been drinking again.

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:07.680
Oh, why won't you let liquor alone?

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:10.090
You know well enough why I drink, Miriam.

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.610
If you'd only give me some encouragement.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.000
I'd like you.

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:15.620
You know that.

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:16.360
Sure, I know.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:18.160
The way you like everything around here.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.780
That isn't what I want, Miriam.

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:21.060
Quiet.

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:22.210
You'll awaken him.

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:24.020
On us now, please go away.

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:25.100
He needs rest.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:40.310
Why didn't you come right back and report?

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:42.790
You know you can depend on me.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.260
You won't have to worry about him anymore.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:49.000
He's at the bottom of that sand pit at Satan's pass, what's left of him.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:54.710
It ought to be worth a lot more than this, seeing as how important Abbott was to you.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:02.710
Thank you.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:03.660
Stop that noise.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:06.200
All right.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:28.660
It's an unusual looking blanket.

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:29.970
with not a

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.200
You like it? It's a poncho.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:32.670
Here's one.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.360
It's woven so your head can go through here.

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:39.210
Our men wear them on the high ranges.

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:41.130
It gets mighty cold up in the plateaus.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.580
beautiful colors

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:44.530
When we make the dyes ourselves.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:45.630
You do?

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:46.600
How?

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:50.220
From roots, flowers, rocks, even from insects.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:53.340
You people seem to be able to do almost anything.

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:54.660
We have to.

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.150
Almost everything we use here, we make ourselves.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:01.400
Miriam.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.040
Soap and water, please.

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:04.080
Yes, Father.

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:07.560
Excuse me.

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:08.190
Sure.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:21.900
Orton doesn't seem to like me.

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:23.580
Can't blame him, can ya?

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:27.410
You know, he'd give his right arm if Miriam worried over him.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.510
as much as she has over you.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.460
But he doesn't seem to be any too fond of you, either.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.620
You got a keen eye, ain't ya?

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.330
No, I don't trust him.

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:39.500
Bad blood.

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:46.600
Noe's father was a rum runner, used to cheat the Indians out of their ponies and blankets by giving them bad whiskey.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:50.200
Cousin Andy picked him up when he was a little shaver.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:51.480
Gave him a home.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:53.980
He thinks he's the salt of the earth.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.180
I'm gonna make something out of it.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:59.900
But I'm thinking you can't make a lily white dove.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.720
out of a desert hawk.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:10.510
Hey!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:24.980
You stay here, Maria.

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:31.680
You

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:41.850
Nebraska.

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:44.440
No trouble this time, Davey.

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:46.680
No holding this rider ever came here without bringing trouble.

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:47.760
That's enough, David.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:53.800
Hey, boss is raising the ante on you this year, Andy.

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:56.140
He wants a thousand head of steer.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:57.510
A thousand?

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.100
Is he crazy?

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:00.660
Well...

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:05.770
It figures that the use of this oasis and the land and water on the West Range is worth it.

00:20:05.980 --> 00:20:07.920
Well, we found that water on the West Range,

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.040
and we opened the seeping wells to us.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:13.290
Holden has claimed it all belongs to the Irish company.

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:16.080
You don't have to argue it out with him.

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:16.850
Hold on.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:20.540
Every time the nabs find rich range in new water...

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:21.770
He claims it for his company.

00:20:22.390 --> 00:20:23.610
Who does Holderness work for?

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:26.000
Who's behind that carefully concealed company?

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:28.260
that he always blames for his lawless actions.

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:29.950
Well, you're guessing.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:35.800
as good as mine well you go back and tell him that i live by the old law that says render unto

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:41.720
every man that which is his but i'm going to fight the claim of his company to the west range and

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:47.060
seeping wells and until the boundary is legally decided i'm not going to pay him a thing for the

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:56.440
use yeah i'll tell him andy but i'm warning you're friendly like you better think it over

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:13.090
Where are you?

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:16.080
You don't seem to be on very good terms with your landlord.

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:17.150
No.

