00:45:55.500 --> 00:45:55.920
Maybe.

00:45:57.220 --> 00:45:58.340
You know why I like you?

00:45:59.050 --> 00:45:59.910
You're the first cook.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:02.940
Look who I ever met who's more curious, sir, than me.

00:46:04.200 --> 00:46:05.400
Come on, let's go.

00:46:28.110 --> 00:46:29.870
Nebraska ain't doing that just for exercise.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:30.220
guys.

00:46:30.920 --> 00:46:32.080
Unless I miss my guests.

00:46:32.330 --> 00:46:34.910
Old Hank Holderness is fixing himself a hideout.

00:46:35.120 --> 00:46:36.200
Again, the day of judgment.

00:47:00.020 --> 00:47:01.620
town, Pastor, where'd you want to see me?

00:47:02.140 --> 00:47:04.740
You got any better sense than to be riding in here in broad daylight?

00:47:05.240 --> 00:47:06.640
I made sure the course was clear.

00:47:07.220 --> 00:47:07.960
What's on your mind?

00:47:08.120 --> 00:47:09.140
We can't talk here.

00:47:09.360 --> 00:47:10.500
Go ahead and talk.

00:47:11.160 --> 00:47:13.620
There ain't been a sign of life around this place in more than an hour.

00:47:16.950 --> 00:47:18.430
How would you like to make a couple of hundred dollars?

00:47:20.590 --> 00:47:22.510
Depends on how much work I have to do to earn it.

00:47:24.630 --> 00:47:26.870
That rock thick has been getting in my way around here.

00:47:27.510 --> 00:47:27.810
yeah

00:47:28.730 --> 00:47:29.630
I heard about him.

00:47:31.300 --> 00:47:32.020
And all the money.

00:47:33.700 --> 00:47:34.500
I wonder now

00:47:35.850 --> 00:47:36.510
You get the rest.

00:47:37.190 --> 00:47:37.650
have to

00:47:38.410 --> 00:47:38.910
Where is he?

00:47:40.330 --> 00:47:41.670
He's up in Crimson Glory Meadows.

00:47:43.180 --> 00:47:43.760
I'll find him.

00:48:03.610 --> 00:48:06.170
Hey, Nebraska, what's the best way to get up to the criminal barring?

00:48:06.390 --> 00:48:10.470
Well, if we don't know the short trail, it's best to go around them by Satan's pass.

00:48:11.350 --> 00:48:12.290
Are they heading up that far?

00:48:13.050 --> 00:48:14.070
A little job to do.

00:48:15.100 --> 00:48:16.940
Who wouldn't want to get it in the back this time?

00:48:17.880 --> 00:48:18.600
A lot bigger.

00:48:34.500 --> 00:48:36.340
Oh, Miss Nile! Oh, Miss Nile!

00:49:05.050 --> 00:49:06.370
Jack, you've got to get away from here.

00:49:06.590 --> 00:49:06.870
Why?

00:49:07.030 --> 00:49:07.990
Chick Chance is coming up here.

00:49:08.090 --> 00:49:08.670
He's going to kill you.

00:49:09.080 --> 00:49:10.540
What for? Who's Chick-Chan's?

00:49:10.540 --> 00:49:11.500
One holding this man.

00:49:11.770 --> 00:49:13.270
A fella with a smile like a knife.

00:49:13.440 --> 00:49:14.320
Always whistling.

00:49:20.220 --> 00:49:21.780
I think I know the gentleman.

00:49:22.710 --> 00:49:24.190
Well, he's coming around by Satan's pass.

00:49:24.600 --> 00:49:25.400
Oh, Jack, please.

00:49:25.780 --> 00:49:26.680
Please get out of here.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:30.380
Yes.

00:49:31.110 --> 00:49:31.850
Yes, I'd better go.

00:49:32.390 --> 00:49:34.110
Ride down to the Oasis. You'll be safe there.

00:49:39.020 --> 00:49:39.240
Action.

00:49:45.480 --> 00:49:46.440
He's riding toward the pass!

00:49:46.730 --> 00:49:47.030
Yeah.

00:49:47.780 --> 00:49:50.980
I never saw such a fella for riding into the wrong places.

00:50:42.600 --> 00:50:43.620
Remember me, Mr. Chance?

00:50:45.960 --> 00:50:46.260
Are you?

00:50:47.300 --> 00:50:48.060
You're John Abbott.

00:50:48.740 --> 00:50:49.100
Yeah.

00:50:50.280 --> 00:50:50.820
What's the matter?

00:50:51.300 --> 00:50:52.240
Forgotten how to whistle?

00:51:31.820 --> 00:51:33.360
I just wish you hadn't come up here today, Miriam.

00:51:34.060 --> 00:51:35.220
I'll miss you more than ever now.

00:51:37.190 --> 00:51:38.250
I'll miss you too, Jack.

00:51:39.240 --> 00:51:41.240
This afternoon has been the happiest I've ever known.

00:51:58.280 --> 00:51:58.720
What's up?

00:51:59.430 --> 00:51:59.830
I wrote up.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.340
I'll tell you the news, Jack, but I guess Miriam's beat me to it.

00:52:04.180 --> 00:52:04.640
What is it?

00:52:06.390 --> 00:52:08.950
My father sent me to carry the word to the Aritar ranches.

00:52:11.100 --> 00:52:11.540
Hot word.

00:52:13.300 --> 00:52:14.600
Hasn't she told you that...

00:52:15.510 --> 00:52:17.230
He's going to marry Snap Thornton two weeks from today.

00:52:21.980 --> 00:52:23.160
I'll go with you in a minute, Davy.

00:52:26.940 --> 00:52:27.280
Miriam.

00:52:28.180 --> 00:52:29.060
It isn't true, is it?

00:52:30.410 --> 00:52:31.110
Jack, they're...

00:52:31.300 --> 00:52:32.900
some forces too strong to fight.

00:52:34.150 --> 00:52:35.230
What do you mean? What forces?

00:52:36.550 --> 00:52:38.950
All my life I've been taught to obey my father's every wish.

00:52:39.910 --> 00:52:41.110
It's too late to change now.

00:52:41.670 --> 00:52:41.870
Cut.

00:52:42.410 --> 00:52:44.930
But he can't marry you off to someone you don't love.

00:52:45.070 --> 00:52:46.290
It isn't fair. It isn't right.

00:52:46.760 --> 00:52:48.260
He made a promise to snap and...

00:52:48.840 --> 00:52:50.320
Right or wrong, it must be kept.

00:52:54.410 --> 00:52:55.590
And I thought you loved me.

00:52:58.020 --> 00:52:58.440
I do.

00:52:59.140 --> 00:52:59.820
You know that.

00:53:01.240 --> 00:53:04.820
Oh, please try to understand. I can't bring more trouble to my father now.

00:53:05.560 --> 00:53:06.220
Don't you see?

00:53:06.940 --> 00:53:08.680
I see he doesn't care what he does to you.

00:53:08.780 --> 00:53:10.100
Don't say anything unkind, please.

00:53:12.790 --> 00:53:13.870
I'll never forget you, Jack.

00:53:15.640 --> 00:53:15.920
Never.

00:53:34.820 --> 00:53:35.440
Where are you going?

00:53:36.360 --> 00:53:38.020
What difference does it make? I'm getting out of here.

00:53:38.820 --> 00:53:40.920
So are you going to quit without trying, huh?

00:53:41.450 --> 00:53:43.410
Running away from this thing you want most.

00:53:44.260 --> 00:53:47.580
Why didn't you just grab her, throw her on a horse and run off with her?

00:53:49.460 --> 00:53:52.160
Oh, maybe you're scared of snap, is that it?

00:53:52.180 --> 00:53:53.440
No, I'm not scared of snap.

00:53:53.600 --> 00:53:55.220
Well, then you're scared of Andy Nabb.

00:53:55.380 --> 00:53:56.660
Oh, go away, nosy.

00:53:57.000 --> 00:53:59.660
Well, what's the matter with you? Are you a man or a mouse?

00:54:00.380 --> 00:54:02.780
A mouse, I reckon, or you wouldn't be quitting so easy.

00:54:03.420 --> 00:54:05.380
Are the nabs any better than the abbots?

00:54:07.420 --> 00:54:08.720
How did you know my name's Abbott?

00:54:08.820 --> 00:54:10.640
Oh, just kind of accidental-like.

00:54:10.720 --> 00:54:12.660
Some letters fell out of your pocket one day

00:54:12.660 --> 00:54:15.260
when you were sick and I was taking care of your clothes.

00:54:15.400 --> 00:54:17.060
Now, listen, I know who you are.

00:54:17.400 --> 00:54:20.320
And I know who owns all the air, so shut up.

00:54:21.690 --> 00:54:27.710
Don't you know that women always have to do just so much blah-blahing and boo-hooing when they're stuck on a fella?

00:54:29.020 --> 00:54:30.000
You know, women all...

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:32.940
I always like to feel noble and self-sacrificing.

00:54:33.740 --> 00:54:39.980
That's just so that afterwards they can say, I told you so, if things don't pan out just like they expected.

00:54:41.800 --> 00:54:45.460
You know, the trouble with Miriam is she's scared you'll get hurt again.

00:54:45.930 --> 00:54:48.130
If you and Snap lock horns over her.

00:54:48.780 --> 00:54:49.120
Yeah.

00:54:50.180 --> 00:54:53.140
She's washed your face and tucked your bib in so long now,

00:54:53.460 --> 00:54:56.960
she figures you ain't got mustard enough to take care of yourself even yet.

00:54:58.310 --> 00:54:59.450
And I guess you ain't.

00:54:59.780 --> 00:55:00.000
Hit.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:00.620
Is that so?

00:55:01.140 --> 00:55:05.060
Well, I'm going to stick around here and see that wedding and be the first to congratulate the happy couple.

00:55:05.200 --> 00:55:07.360
Hold on now. You ain't aiming to start something.

00:55:07.500 --> 00:55:08.560
I'll even give her a wedding present.

00:55:09.560 --> 00:55:10.500
two weeks from today.

00:55:11.380 --> 00:55:13.880
That's just time enough to get a letter to Chicago and back.

00:55:30.250 --> 00:55:30.550
Hey!

00:55:34.120 --> 00:55:35.340
Is there a letter here for John Abbott?

00:55:35.720 --> 00:55:36.080
No.

00:56:00.440 --> 00:56:05.060
Maybe you haven't heard, Holderness, but opening other people's mail is a penitentiary offence.

00:56:05.530 --> 00:56:08.410
I represent the Arata company, an abbot since he's dead.

00:56:10.520 --> 00:56:12.220
Pretty sure of Abbott's death, aren't you?

00:56:13.530 --> 00:56:15.910
Even a man like Chick Chance slips up once in a while.

00:56:17.750 --> 00:56:18.610
I'm John Abbott.

00:56:21.780 --> 00:56:22.500
I'll take care of that.

00:56:32.650 --> 00:56:33.450
You're a notary, aren't you?

00:56:33.630 --> 00:56:34.290
Yes, certainly.

00:56:35.910 --> 00:56:36.790
Notarize my signature.

00:56:46.920 --> 00:56:47.600
Take it easy, boys.

00:56:48.320 --> 00:56:51.480
What? What's the... What's the... What's the... What's going on in there?

00:56:51.520 --> 00:56:54.200
I don't mind what's going on. Unbuckle those guns and drop them.

00:57:03.320 --> 00:57:03.840
It ain't there.

00:57:07.900 --> 00:57:08.160
Bravo!

00:57:12.820 --> 00:57:17.320
This is a grantee transferring certain properties in Erita to one Miriam Naev.

00:57:17.500 --> 00:57:18.400
D-d-do you swear?

00:57:18.680 --> 00:57:19.040
Yes.

00:57:20.380 --> 00:57:20.760
Nebraska!

00:57:21.370 --> 00:57:24.190
I'm afraid Nebraska won't be joining us, Mr. Holderness.

00:57:26.070 --> 00:57:27.630
That'll be four bits to make it legal.

00:57:34.760 --> 00:57:38.880
Now I'll just take this record of how you've managed my estate for your own property.

00:57:43.910 --> 00:57:46.090
If I were you, I'd get out of this part of the country.

00:57:47.020 --> 00:57:48.320
before the sheriff gets here.

00:57:50.980 --> 00:57:51.540
Get him inside.

00:57:51.780 --> 00:57:52.800
Come on, get in that room.

00:57:53.130 --> 00:57:53.510
All right, y'all.

00:57:54.380 --> 00:57:54.860
Get him out.

00:57:57.800 --> 00:57:58.400
Take this, nosy.

00:58:07.260 --> 00:58:09.530
Well, looks like we've come to the end of our roof.

00:58:09.750 --> 00:58:10.610
I'm not through yet.

00:58:10.850 --> 00:58:11.590
Break down that door.

00:58:12.100 --> 00:58:13.600
We're riding for Rock Mountain Hideout.

00:59:07.670 --> 00:59:07.870
Okay.

00:59:31.140 --> 00:59:32.120
Well, it's a deed to the Oasis.

00:59:34.630 --> 00:59:36.430
Then you're the owner of the Aritar.

00:59:37.100 --> 00:59:37.460
Yes.

00:59:38.090 --> 00:59:40.070
But I want you to know that whatever Holderness did,

00:59:40.620 --> 00:59:41.620
Wasn't done in my name.

00:59:42.120 --> 00:59:44.500
Why, there's no need for you to tell me that, my boy.

00:59:45.290 --> 00:59:47.210
Well, I'm grateful to you, Jack, but...

00:59:47.850 --> 00:59:48.770
We can't accept this.

00:59:48.870 --> 00:59:49.270
Why not?

00:59:50.760 --> 00:59:52.920
My rights, the Oasis ought to belong to the NAVs anyway.

00:59:56.870 --> 00:59:57.790
you've got a dress day.

01:00:02.100 --> 01:00:02.120
Thank you.

01:00:07.830 --> 01:00:08.810
Thank you.

01:00:39.270 --> 01:00:39.750
Miriam

01:00:45.030 --> 01:00:45.390
Thank you.

01:00:46.060 --> 01:00:47.200
You ain't gonna marry, Snap.

01:00:47.780 --> 01:00:50.420
I ain't gonna let you do something you'll be sorry for all the rest of your life.

01:00:50.600 --> 01:00:52.280
I'm not thinking of myself. You know that.

01:00:52.400 --> 01:00:54.720
Now, don't give me any of them high and noble ideas.

01:00:55.300 --> 01:00:58.540
Snap's not only a drunkard, he's a spying, lying thief.

01:00:59.110 --> 01:00:59.710
What are you saying?

01:01:00.020 --> 01:01:02.220
You heard me. He's all I said he wasn't more.

01:01:02.650 --> 01:01:03.150
Why, listen.

01:01:03.540 --> 01:01:07.120
He's been working for Holderness for years, and I can prove it.

01:01:19.260 --> 01:01:20.900
Here's your horse and here's the open desert.

01:01:21.340 --> 01:01:24.120
It's the last chance you got to get the man you really love.

01:01:24.470 --> 01:01:25.170
Will you take it?

01:01:26.390 --> 01:01:26.990
Yes, I will.

01:01:27.320 --> 01:01:27.680
Oh God.

01:01:38.720 --> 01:01:41.860
Miriam, meet you at the railroad station at Granite Junction.

01:02:06.260 --> 01:02:07.900
She's gone. She's riding out across the desert.

01:02:09.340 --> 01:02:10.480
You had something to do with this.

01:02:11.900 --> 01:02:12.420
Good one.

01:02:17.340 --> 01:02:17.880
Brian, wait!

01:02:18.710 --> 01:02:19.750
Marin's horse is gone.

01:02:22.330 --> 01:02:23.770
You're staying here, Jack.

01:03:31.080 --> 01:03:32.740
We'll hold her in case the nap's starting at him.

01:03:42.890 --> 01:03:43.730
Hello, Miriam.

01:03:49.610 --> 01:03:51.250
What sort of a honeymoon is this, Snap?

01:03:51.750 --> 01:03:52.170
Davey!

01:03:52.430 --> 01:03:53.510
They call that bridle.

01:03:53.610 --> 01:03:55.270
You know of anyone who has a better right to it?

01:03:56.200 --> 01:03:58.600
It looks as if you picked the wrong place to start trouble, man.

01:03:58.840 --> 01:03:59.840
You keep on this holiness.

01:04:00.700 --> 01:04:01.740
My snap's my friend.

01:04:02.160 --> 01:04:03.760
I wouldn't think of standing in his way.

01:04:04.200 --> 01:04:06.660
A wedding is a wedding, with a hell of the Oasis

01:04:06.660 --> 01:04:07.520
or someplace else.

01:04:08.200 --> 01:04:09.260
Please go back, Davey.

01:04:09.660 --> 01:04:10.680
Not without you, Miriam.

01:04:11.440 --> 01:04:11.920
Davey!

01:04:12.100 --> 01:04:12.580
Don't!

01:04:12.800 --> 01:04:16.220
Your father, Davey!

01:04:16.540 --> 01:04:27.230
It's very far.

01:04:30.030 --> 01:04:53.820
All the money hauling this page staff been going on for years.

01:04:53.980 --> 01:04:55.340
We'll write against hauling this Andrew.

01:04:55.520 --> 01:04:57.460
Every one of us has got a score to settle with him.

01:04:57.580 --> 01:04:57.980
Yes, sir.

01:05:01.210 --> 01:05:02.950
Well, maybe this will change your mind.

01:05:03.480 --> 01:05:04.160
Look at that.

01:05:04.660 --> 01:05:06.460
For taking care of Saul Nabb.

01:05:06.820 --> 01:05:07.340
$100.

01:05:08.150 --> 01:05:10.370
Snap Thornton killed your boy Saul.

01:05:16.060 --> 01:05:16.900
Why, David.

01:05:23.830 --> 01:05:28.670
Oh, what's happened?

01:05:30.220 --> 01:05:33.900
It's a bad idea, doesn't it?

01:05:34.280 --> 01:05:37.640
It doesn't hurt enough, Jack.

01:05:39.910 --> 01:05:42.270
Ornest has buried him in the past.

01:05:50.640 --> 01:05:51.140
Who did it?

01:07:30.250 --> 01:07:30.870
To get Miriam.

01:07:32.030 --> 01:07:32.330
Careful.

01:07:41.940 --> 01:07:43.060
You're a justice of the peace.

01:07:43.540 --> 01:07:45.140
This is as good a time as any for the wedding.

01:07:45.520 --> 01:07:48.130
Oh, that can wait until we prepare this place for defense.

01:07:48.860 --> 01:07:49.720
Why, you're safe enough.

01:07:49.740 --> 01:07:50.660
You got this place covered.

01:07:50.920 --> 01:07:52.160
Let's get on with my affairs.

01:07:52.380 --> 01:07:53.200
Now, hold on.

01:07:53.700 --> 01:07:55.860
Justice Quirk says such a marriage won't be legal.

01:07:59.320 --> 01:07:59.980
All right, then, I'm taking...

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:00.740
Now back to the nabs.

01:08:00.990 --> 01:08:02.330
No, you don't, and keep out of there.

01:08:02.590 --> 01:08:03.390
I'm getting out.

01:08:03.860 --> 01:08:04.200
Sure.

01:08:05.010 --> 01:08:05.810
But you're going alone.

01:08:08.020 --> 01:08:08.840
What are you going to do with her?

01:08:10.100 --> 01:08:13.320
If it's any of your business, I'm keeping her here in case Nab writes against me.

01:08:13.380 --> 01:08:14.560
You're lying and you know it.

01:08:14.760 --> 01:08:17.220
You're figuring on marrying me yourself now that she owns the Oasis.

01:08:18.900 --> 01:08:19.920
That's a good idea at that.

01:08:21.050 --> 01:08:21.770
Now get out.

01:08:58.920 --> 01:08:59.400
and be held.

01:09:19.290 --> 01:09:21.170
I'll save your bullet, Andy.

01:09:22.140 --> 01:09:23.760
I ain't got long to live.

01:09:25.020 --> 01:09:26.160
Frightens my business

01:09:27.380 --> 01:09:28.960
Laying the lowdown on women.

01:09:30.220 --> 01:09:31.520
something I can't stem it

01:09:32.970 --> 01:09:34.650
He's in the canyon at the...

01:09:35.400 --> 01:09:36.260
For the rock mountain.

01:09:36.640 --> 01:09:37.340
Get out! Come here!

01:09:52.740 --> 01:09:53.140
Long

01:11:32.490 --> 01:11:33.250
Isn't that liars?

01:12:34.440 --> 01:12:35.420
Thank you.

01:12:37.800 --> 01:12:39.800
Go on, go on, I'll let you have it.

01:12:47.360 --> 01:12:48.520
Go on, go on.

01:13:13.370 --> 01:13:13.770
Beautiful.

01:13:14.870 --> 01:13:16.350
I'll always love this desert, do you?

01:13:17.300 --> 01:13:18.720
It brought me everything I'd ever want.

01:13:24.220 --> 01:13:24.800
Yours and mine.

01:13:26.580 --> 01:13:26.820
out.
